  "note": "Election of the whole Cookstown Urban District Council, polled Wednesday 18 September 1946; twenty candidates for twelve seats (Mid-Ulster Mail, 21 September 1946, p. 4). 'The poll resulted in the election of 9 Official Unionists, 2 Ratepayers' Association candidates and one Independent.' Electorate 1,458; 1,325 voted; 26 spoiled papers; poll 90.8 per cent. The result list was read from the page image because the OCR drops most of the figures."
